         <div type="bio">
            <p>English poet, novelist, and, later, biographer. Assistant Editor of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">The Egoist</name>. While giving <name type="work" key="W_ULYSSES">Ulysses</name> a mixed review (“The Influence of Mr. James Joyce”, <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">English Review</name> 32 [April 1921], 333-41), he harshly dismissed <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Finnegans Wake</name> as “pedantic nonsense” (“The Bookshelf”, <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Atlantic</name> 163, no. 6 [June 1939]). <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
